s ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; It establishes a simple formula for counting these hooks, confirming a conjecture about their divisibility by $t$. ... Source: OpenAlex · Snapshot 23 Sep 2026 ... Paper ID: 2312.02933 ... @article{singh2024hook, title = {Hook lengths in self-conjugate partitions}, author = {Singh, Ajit and Andrews, George E. and Ono, Ken and others}, year = {2024}, eprint = {2312.02933}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }\n$$ As a consequence, if $a_t^*(n)$ is the number of such hooks among the self-conjugate partitions of $n,$ then for even $t$ we obtain the simple formula $$ a_t^*(n)=t\\sum_{j\\geq 1} q^*(n-2tj), $$ where $q^*(m)$ is the number of partitions of $m$ into distinct odd parts. As a corollary, we find that $t\\mid a_t^*(n),$ which confirms a conjecture of Ballantine, Burson, Craig, Folsom, and Wen.\n\n### OpenAlex\n\nCitations in OpenAlex\n    0\n\nPublication year\n    2023\n\nAccess status\n    Open access\n\nView on OpenAlex (opens in a new tab) Read open-access version (opens in a new tab)\n\nSource: OpenAlex · Snapshot 23 Sep 2026\n\n### Impact\n\n13\n\nReferences\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 2312.02933\n\nLicense: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\n\nComments: 12 pages; minor revision based on referee reports\n\nCategories:\n\nmath.CO\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### How to Cite This Paper\n\n[Button: BibTeX] [Button: APA] [Button: MLA] [Button: Chicago] [Button: IEEE]\n\n@article{singh2024hook, title = {Hook lengths in self-conjugate partitions}, author = {Singh, Ajit and Andrews, George E. and Ono, Ken and others}, year = {2024}, eprint = {2312.02933}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }\n\n### Authors\n\nAS Ajit Singh 38 papers GE George E. Andrews 488 papers KO Ken Ono 4 papers TA Tewodros Amdeberhan 124 papers\n\n## Key Terms\n\npartitions (0.407)\n\npartitions (0.396)\n\nlambda (0.337)\n\nlambda (0.327)\n\nsum_ (0.291)\n\nconjugate (0.291)\n\nsum_ (0.281)\n\nconjugate (0.266)